/E (Lasso Regression \(Least Absolute Shrinkage and Selection Operator\) is a regularized linear regression technique that extends Multiple Linear Regression by adding a penalty term to the loss function. Like Ridge Regression, it is used to control model complexity and prevent overfitting. However, Lasso Regression has an additional advantage: it can automatically perform feature selection. In datasets such as USA Housing, not all input variables contribute equally to house price prediction. Some features may have very little influence on the target variable. Lasso Regression helps identify these )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [27]
>>
