/E (The baseline clustering models demonstrated exceptional structural consistency, achieving a nearperfect Adjusted Rand Index of 94.20% between the K-Means and Hierarchical approaches. By utilizing standardized scaling, both algorithms successfully isolated five distinct customer segments, maintaining robust Silhouette Scores of approximately 0.55. This indicates well-defined cluster boundaries and high intra-cluster cohesion relative to inter- cluster separation. Analysis of the Davies-Bouldin Index, which remained below 0.58 for both models, further )
/Pg 91 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
