/Title (Using high-level libraries like Keras and TensorFlow simplifies the creation, training, and evaluation of ANNs. Keras provides an intuitive, user-friendly API to define layers, choose activation functions, and compile models with  different loss functions and optimizers, while TensorFlow handles the underlying computations efficiently on CPUs or GPUs. This combination allows developers to experiment with different architectures, such as feedforward networks, convolutional networks for image processing, or recurrent networks for sequential data. With built-in functions for data preprocessing, model evaluation, and visualization, Keras and TensorFlow enable rapid prototyping and deployment of neural networks, making advanced machine learning techniques more accessible to both researchers and industry practitioners.)
